  What Notification hooks are for:
  They fire when Claude Code sends a notification (e.g., waiting for input, task complete). They're typically used for
  desktop alerts, not file formatting.

  Example working Notification hook (Windows):
  {
    "Notification": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "powershell -Command \"[System.Reflection.Assembly]::LoadWithPartialName('System.Windows.Forms');
   [System.Windows.Forms.MessageBox]::Show('Claude needs attention!')\""
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }

  Would you like me to:
  1. Add a desktop notification hook - Shows a popup when Claude needs your attention
  2. Add a sound alert hook - Plays a beep when Claude is waiting
  3. Something else - Tell me what you'd like the notification hook to do

