> how to do this in command prompt

● In Windows Command Prompt, use the dir command:

  dir "C:\Users\SriniAchuthan\OneDrive\Desktop\Angular JS\typescript"

  Common options:
  ┌──────────┬──────────────────────────┐
  │ Command  │       Description        │
  ├──────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ dir      │ List files and folders   │
  ├──────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ dir /a   │ Show hidden files too    │
  ├──────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ dir /s   │ Include subdirectories   │
  ├──────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ dir /b   │ Bare format (names only) │
  ├──────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ dir /o:n │ Sort by name             │
  ├──────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ dir /o:d │ Sort by date             │
  └──────────┴──────────────────────────┘
  Examples:
  # List all files including hidden
  dir /a "C:\path\to\folder"

  # List only filenames
  dir /b "C:\path\to\folder"

  # List files in all subdirectories
  dir /s "C:\path\to\folder"

